+# Design analysis for the D10 variant
+# ----------------------------------
+# spec_variant:
+#   unchanged_core_rule:
+#     - input still has a 6x24 top legend whose colored bars encode left/right turns
+#     - main grid still has one solid teal square and 3-4 edge-touching obstacle rectangles
+#     - four sz-wide teal beams still slide from the square, turn on obstacle hit, and stop at edges
+#   changed_output_rule:
+#     - original solver returned the entire main region after removing the legend
+#     - this variant returns only the minimum bounding rectangle of the final teal trace
+#     - "trace" means every teal-painted beam cell plus the teal source square
+#     - obstacle/background cells inside that rectangle remain; anything outside it is discarded
+#   concrete_behavior_trace:
+#     - original flow: parse legend -> simulate beams on full main grid -> return full painted main grid
+#     - new flow: parse legend -> simulate beams on full main grid -> find bbox of all teal cells -> crop to that bbox
+#     - difference appears after painting, not during beam motion or obstacle parsing
+#   hidden_assumption_audit:
+#     - rows_with_legend assumes color 5 appears only in the top band; generator still guarantees this
+#     - _find_teal_square assumes exactly one solid teal square exists in the uncropped main area; unchanged
+#     - obstacle_color_at_next assumes a beam footprint never intersects mixed obstacle colors; generator still prevents overlap
+#     - the old return out silently assumed the desired output kept all non-trajectory margins; this is the key invalidated assumption
+#     - new crop assumes at least one teal cell exists after simulation; guaranteed by the source square itself
+#   placement_legality:
+#     - generation still places the square away from edges and obstacles with no overlap
+#     - after simulation, cropping may cut away empty margins and may also trim obstacle parts that lie fully outside the teal bbox
+#     - this is legal because the new output rule is defined purely by the trace extent
+#   observability:
+#     - if the trace touched all four sides, the crop would degenerate to the old full main grid and D10 would be invisible
+#     - generator therefore keeps only samples where the trace bbox is strictly smaller in both height and width
+#     - the specific cropped sides vary by sample, so the solver cannot hard-code one side or one fixed offset
+#   cleanliness:
+#     - only one overlay layer is added: teal beam paint over the original base
+#     - the crop is axis-aligned and uses the trace itself, so the output remains visually tidy and readable
+
